  "body": "Spec: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/#hidden-elements\r\n\r\nThe spec claims that there's a default UA style of:\r\n```css\r\n/* ... */ source, track { display: none; }\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut based on this test:\r\n```html\r\n<script>\r\nwindow.onload = function () {\r\n  'area, base, basefont, datalist, head, link, meta, noembed, noframes, param, rp, script, source, style, template, track, title'.split(', ').forEach(function (tagName) {\r\n    var tag = document.createElement(tagName);\r\n    tag.appendChild(document.createTextNode(tagName + ' '));\r\n    document.body.appendChild(tag);\r\n  });\r\n};\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\nChrome, Safari, and Firefox don't have such a default style, contrary to the spec. (I don't have Edge handy to test against.)",
